    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d352">

                <pb facs="0435" n="323" xml:id="pg323"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/3566: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reinsch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                            notAfter="1919-01-03T09:40:00-05:00"
                            notBefore="1919-01-02T00:00:00+04:53"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received January 3, 1919, 9:40
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Following from [Harris at] Omsk.</p>
                <p>“2. 2d. Foreign Office here states that it has received telegram from former
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs Sazonoff that Denikin has recognized the Kolchak
                    government. Harris.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
